Package: libkeel1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: keel-common (= ${source:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Keel robot baseboard library
 libkeel drives the Keel robot baseboard on a Raspberry Pi 4: two motors
 behind a hardware enable gate, the safety MCU's heartbeat and arming
 handshake, six RGB LEDs, four buttons with indicator LEDs and the
 ultrasonic ranging connector. A built-in simulator runs the same safety
 state machine against the production MCU policy.
 .
 This package contains the shared library libkeel.so.1 (ABI 1.0), which C
 programs and the Python and Java bindings load.

Package: libkeel-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libkeel1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Keel robot baseboard library (development files)
 libkeel drives the Keel robot baseboard on a Raspberry Pi 4 and offers a
 simulator of the board and its safety MCU.
 .
 This package contains the headers keel/keel.h and keel/port.h, the static
 library, the CMake package Keel (Keel::keel, Keel::keel_static) and the
 pkg-config files keel.pc and keel-static.pc. The camera library's
 development files are in libkeel-camera-dev.

Package: libkeel-camera1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libcamera-ipa,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Keel robot camera library
 libkeel-camera drives the camera of a Keel robot: Camera Module 2 and
 Camera Module 3 (and other cameras libcamera supports) on a Raspberry
 Pi 4, through libcamera and the Pi's hardware H.264 and JPEG encoders.
 Programs read raw frames or encoded chunks, take stills, record files
 and stream over TCP and UDP. It does not need libkeel1.
 .
 This package contains the shared library libkeel-camera.so.1 (ABI 1.0),
 which C programs and the Python and Java bindings load.

Package: libkeel-camera-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libkeel-camera1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libkeel-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Keel robot camera library (development files)
 libkeel-camera drives the camera of a Keel robot through libcamera and the
 Raspberry Pi's hardware encoders.
 .
 This package contains the header keel/camera.h, the link
 libkeel-camera.so, the CMake target Keel::keel_camera
 (find_package(Keel COMPONENTS camera)) and the pkg-config file
 keel-camera.pc.

Package: keel-common
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: kmod,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Keel robot baseboard system integration
 Device access and scheduling for libkeel: a udev rule that gives the
 Raspberry Pi 4 GPIO chip and I2C1 to the distribution's gpio and i2c
 groups (or to the keel group where those do not exist), the keel system
 group, a modules-load entry for i2c-dev and a real-time priority limit of
 40 for the keel group. It never edits the boot configuration and never
 adds users to groups; keel-setup does that on request.

Package: keel-tools
Section: utils
Architecture: any
Depends: libkeel1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Keel robot baseboard tools
 Tools for the Keel robot baseboard: keel-setup prepares a Raspberry Pi 4
 (group membership, SPI0 off and I2C1 on in a marked, backed-up block of
 config.txt), keel-doctor checks device access, the GPIO lines, the
 real-time limits and I2C, and keel-live and keel-demo exercise the board.

Package: keel-camera
Section: video
Architecture: any
Depends: libkeel-camera1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Keel robot camera tool
 keel-camera lists the cameras of a Keel robot, takes stills, records,
 streams over TCP and UDP and writes raw frames to standard output, through
 libkeel-camera.
